 "building": "family house",
 "description": "The main dwelling. A C-shaped house of 14 x 14 m wrapping a 6 x 10 m courtyard that opens west to the sunset, with the base band along the road. Three stepped floors follow the hill. One arm runs open to its roof at 4.6-4.9 m; the other carries a second floor with the master suite, dressing, 3 x 3 bath and a 4 x 4 open terrace, plus the platform over the base band. NOTE: at 136 m2 of ground coverage this exceeds the 90 m2 cap. It stands as the design intent; whether it can be built depends on the building-count question in thai-hillside-law."
